{comment: Intro}
G (B-A-B-A B-B-A B-D D) (B-A-B-A B-B-A B-G G) (2x)

{comment: Verse}
Em C G/D Bm 7
Jesus came and loved me, took my sin to Calvary, He has made a way for me.
[Em]Now my eyes are open, si[Cm]nce I’ve come to know Him. Hi[G/D]s great love has set me f[Dsus]ree.

{comment: Chorus}
G Em 7
1. At the cross, my debt was paid, all my sins were washed away.
2. At the cross, my Savior died, shed His blood, was crucified.
D G/B* C G *do not play during solo Chorus
1. Just for me, amazing grace at the cross.
2. Just for me, He gave His life at the cross.

{comment: Bridge}
{ci: Unison}
C G D Em 7 C G D
My joy will ever be in the One who saved me, Jesus, Lamb of Calvary.
All praises to the King for His grace and mercy. I have been redeemed.

{comment: Bridge}
{ci: Parts}
1 st line same as before
C G Em 7 D Em 7 C G/B Em 7 D
All praises to the King for His grace and mercy. I have been redeemed.
{ci: Return to Chorus; cut music for the first half; repeat last line twice to end}
